* Added Windows zero-touch onboarding. On a Windows image that auto-logs-in a temporary `fleet-provision` account, fleetd runs the setup experience in a full-screen Edge kiosk, asks the end user to choose a password, creates a standard local account from their IdP identity, disables the provisioning account, and opens Windows Hello sign-in options at the user's first sign-in. If the image includes a Microsoft Entra bulk-join provisioning package, fleetd joins the device to Entra instead of creating a local account, and the end user signs in with their Entra account.
